      "rationale": "Every DST-transition date has exactly 1440 logger rows, yet the intraday grid-voltage profile does not move across any transition (median |shift| 0 min; a logger ignoring DST would show ~60 min). The logger therefore follows the Europe/Paris wall clock and the published file was re-gridded to 1440 rows/day. On spring-forward days the non-existent 02:00-02:59 rows are exact copies of 03:00-03:59 (2007-03-25: 98%, 2008-03-30: 98%, 2009-03-29: 98%, 2010-03-28: 98% identical), so they are dropped. On autumn days the repeated 02:00-02:59 hour appears only once and cannot be attributed to either occurrence, so those rows are dropped too and both UTC hours become missing. No hour is shifted or guessed."
    },
